    "title": "National Puppy Day: Illinois Patch Celebrates Pups Of All Ages",
    "text": "Skip to main contentChicago, ILLincoln Park, ILBucktown-Wicker Park, ILLakeview, ILNorth Center-Roscoe Village, ILHyde Park, ILWest Side, ILSouth Side, ILLincoln Square, ILOak Park-River Forest, ILIllinoisTop National NewsSee All CommunitiesILLINOIS — To celebrate National Puppy Day, March 23, we asked Patch readers from across Illinois to share pics of their beloved dogs with us. There was no age minimum; in fact, the only limit was a dog's level of cuteness. And, though each of these puppies exceeded our official cuteness level by billions of puppymeters, they're all featured in our 2026 National Puppy Day roundup. At the very bottom of the page, you'll find some cute dogs* who warm the hearts of your local Patch Editors! Enjoy! via Becky Klein, Nicole Bruce, Bonnie Pace, Gary Latman, Britt Utrata, Lori Raasch, Gloria Nowotarski, Gary Klecka via Maryellen Bilek, Jennifer Stratton, Julia Garcia Roch, Cindy Goluszka, Jamie Viebach, Dawson Lavelle, Graesen Arnoff, Jerry Zabin via Edward Alicea, Rosemarie Garcia, Jim Johnson, Lee Gundersheimer, Trish Wolfe Anton, Geisha Ester, Cathy and Bill Welch, Debbie McCormac, Tracey Krueger via via Maureen O’Connell, Joanna Bisgrove, Mark Telpner, Emma Welliver, Brian Jones, Kristen Kozik, Peg O’Leary, Michelle Montgomery, Bethany Mullen via Tim Strejc, Mary Pirc, Michael Zupancic, Andrea Jawor, Robert Bolek, Jane Schneider, Madonna Walsh via Lorraine Swanson, Lisa Farver, Shannon Antinori *The term dog is used loosely here to apply to a cat who behaves very much like a dog and belongs to Senior Editor, Lorraine Swanson, who was formerly only a \"dog person\" before she adopted Frehley. Find out what's happening in Across Illinoisfor free with the latest updates from Patch.Get more local news delivered straight to your inbox. Sign up for free Patch newsletters and alerts.",
